// Title: VM inventory for reservation coverage (size, power state, priority, region)
// Purpose: Input for reservation / savings plan sizing: every VM with its size, region and priority (Regular vs Spot).
// Source table(s): Azure Resource Graph, resources (microsoft.compute/virtualmachines)
// Parameters to edit: none. Join with the scale set query (vmss-inventory-for-reservations.kql).
// Notes/traps: compare reservations by instance size flexibility group (ISF units), not by raw VM
//          count, a reservation for one size covers a ratio of related sizes. Spot VMs
//          (priority = Spot) are not covered by reservations. powerState is needed to see which VMs
//          actually run, a deallocated VM consumes no compute but still shows up here.
resources
| where type =~ 'microsoft.compute/virtualmachines'
| where isnotempty(tostring(properties.hardwareProfile.vmSize))
| project id, name, size = tostring(properties.hardwareProfile.vmSize),
    power = tostring(properties.extended.instanceView.powerState.code),
    priority = tostring(properties.priority),
    location, subscriptionId
